<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" title="In C.3 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs and Derivations ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Part 2: Proof of <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=0]=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=0]=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A3.SS4" title="In Appendix C Proofs and Derivations ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">C.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <span class="ltx_ref"></span></span></a></li>
</ol></li>
