</figure>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix A More Experimental Results ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Appendix A More Experimental Results ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the conclusion in the main paper remains the same: our method can still obtain the best results with both synthetic and real-world noise.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We describe how to integrate Algorithm 1 (backward, unbiased reward de-biasing) and Algorithm 2 (forward, gradient-scaled) into <em id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Group Relative Policy Optimization</em> (GRPO) under both <em id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">outcome</em> and <em id="A2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">process</em> supervision. GRPO samples, for each prompt <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, a group of <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> responses <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> from the behavior policy, computes a <em id="A2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">group-normalized advantage</em> for each sample (or step), and then applies a PPO-style clipped surrogate with a separate KL regularizer to a reference policy; no value network is used. Our modifications are confined to the advantage-construction stage, leaving ratio clipping and KL loss unchanged (details of GRPO in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024b</a>)</cite> and open-source implementations).</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation (shared).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> be the current policy and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> the behavior policy. Define token-level ratios <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i,t}=\tfrac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\!\mid x,y_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\mathrm{old}}(y_{i,t}\!\mid x,y_{i,&lt;t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i,t}=\tfrac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\!\mid x,y_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\mathrm{old}}(y_{i,t}\!\mid x,y_{i,&lt;t})}</annotation></semantics></math>. GRPO’s PPO-style surrogate at token <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> uses an advantage <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{grpo}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\frac{1}{|y_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\min\!\big(r_{i,t}\,A_{i,t},\ \mathrm{clip}(r_{i,t},1\!\pm\!\varepsilon)\,A_{i,t}\big)\ -\ \beta\,\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>grpo</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>clip</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mpadded style="width:0.108em;" width="0.108em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.052em">±</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{grpo}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\frac{1}{|y_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\min\!\big(r_{i,t}\,A_{i,t},\ \mathrm{clip}(r_{i,t},1\!\pm\!\varepsilon)\,A_{i,t}\big)\ -\ \beta\,\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the KL term is added to the loss rather than folded into the reward. Our corrections only change how <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is formed.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Outcome Supervision (one scalar reward per response)</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we observe a binary verifier reward <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}_{i}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{i}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algo 1 (Backward) in GRPO.</span> First construct an <em id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unbiased</em> per-sample reward</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}_{i}\;=\;\frac{\tilde{r}_{i}-\hat{\rho}_{0}}{\,1-\hat{\rho}_{0}-\hat{\rho}_{1}\,}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}_{i}\;=\;\frac{\tilde{r}_{i}-\hat{\rho}_{0}}{\,1-\hat{\rho}_{0}-\hat{\rho}_{1}\,}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Compute group statistics on <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\widehat{r}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\widehat{r}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{r}\;=\;\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\widehat{r}_{i},\qquad s\;=\;\sqrt{\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}(\widehat{r}_{i}-\bar{r})^{2}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{r}\;=\;\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\widehat{r}_{i},\qquad s\;=\;\sqrt{\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}(\widehat{r}_{i}-\bar{r})^{2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Define the group-normalized advantage <em id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">constant across tokens</em> of the same response,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{i}^{\text{(back)}}\;=\;\frac{\widehat{r}_{i}-\bar{r}}{\,s+\varepsilon\,},\qquad A_{i,t}\;\equiv\;a_{i}^{\text{(back)}},\ \forall t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>(back)</mtext></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">≡</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>(back)</mtext></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{\text{(back)}}\;=\;\frac{\widehat{r}_{i}-\bar{r}}{\,s+\varepsilon\,},\qquad A_{i,t}\;\equiv\;a_{i}^{\text{(back)}},\ \forall t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">This is a drop-in replacement for the usual GRPO outcome-advantage, with the sole change being that the group mean/variance are computed over de-noised rewards <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> rather than raw <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algo 2 (Forward) in GRPO.</span> First form the <em id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">standard</em> GRPO outcome-advantage from the <em id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">observed</em> rewards:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{i}\;=\;\frac{\tilde{r}_{i}-\overline{\tilde{r}}}{\,\mathrm{std}(\{\tilde{r}_{j}\})+\varepsilon\,},\qquad A_{i,t}\;\equiv\;a_{i},\ \forall t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>std</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">≡</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\;=\;\frac{\tilde{r}_{i}-\overline{\tilde{r}}}{\,\mathrm{std}(\{\tilde{r}_{j}\})+\varepsilon\,},\qquad A_{i,t}\;\equiv\;a_{i},\ \forall t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Then apply the forward weight determined only by <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\rho}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\rho}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}\;=\;\begin{cases}\hat{\rho}_{1}-1,&amp;\tilde{r}_{i}=0,\\
\hat{\rho}_{1},&amp;\tilde{r}_{i}=1,\end{cases}\qquad A_{i,t}\ \leftarrow\ w_{i}\cdot A_{i,t}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}\;=\;\begin{cases}\hat{\rho}_{1}-1,&amp;\tilde{r}_{i}=0,\\
\hat{\rho}_{1},&amp;\tilde{r}_{i}=1,\end{cases}\qquad A_{i,t}\ \leftarrow\ w_{i}\cdot A_{i,t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, the group-normalization is a positive scaling of each sample’s (token-shared) factor, so multiplying by <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> implements the same gradient scaling as in REINFORCE, but expressed at the advantage level that GRPO’s surrogate consumes. The rest of GRPO (ratio clipping, KL loss) is unchanged.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Process Supervision (step-wise rewards)</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose each response <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> has step indices <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{index}_{i}(1)&lt;\cdots&lt;\mathrm{index}_{i}(K_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>index</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>index</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{index}_{i}(1)&lt;\cdots&lt;\mathrm{index}_{i}(K_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> with step-level observed rewards <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> attached at those indices. GRPO forms step-normalized rewards and turns them into token advantages by backward accumulation over steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algo 1 (Backward) in GRPO-Process.</span> De-noise each step reward:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}_{i}^{(j)}\;=\;\frac{\tilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}-\hat{\rho}_{0}}{\,1-\hat{\rho}_{0}-\hat{\rho}_{1}\,}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}_{i}^{(j)}\;=\;\frac{\tilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}-\hat{\rho}_{0}}{\,1-\hat{\rho}_{0}-\hat{\rho}_{1}\,}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Normalize across the <em id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">group and steps</em> in the current batch following GRPO’s process recipe:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}\;=\;\frac{\widehat{r}_{i}^{(j)}-\mathrm{mean}(\{\widehat{r}_{\ell}^{(m)}\})}{\,\mathrm{std}(\{\widehat{r}_{\ell}^{(m)}\})+\varepsilon\,}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>mean</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>std</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}\;=\;\frac{\widehat{r}_{i}^{(j)}-\mathrm{mean}(\{\widehat{r}_{\ell}^{(m)}\})}{\,\mathrm{std}(\{\widehat{r}_{\ell}^{(m)}\})+\varepsilon\,}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Accumulate into token-level advantages (for all tokens <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> at or before the <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th step boundary):</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i,t}\;=\;\sum_{\mathrm{index}_{i}(j)\geq t}\ \widetilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>index</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i,t}\;=\;\sum_{\mathrm{index}_{i}(j)\geq t}\ \widetilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">This mirrors the standard GRPO-Process pipeline, but with <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algo 2 (Forward) in GRPO-Process.</span> First follow the <em id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">standard</em> GRPO-Process normalization to obtain <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> from the <em id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">observed</em> <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, then accumulate the token advantages</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i,t}\;=\;\sum_{\mathrm{index}_{i}(j)\geq t}\ \widetilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>index</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i,t}\;=\;\sum_{\mathrm{index}_{i}(j)\geq t}\ \widetilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and finally apply forward weights. If the verifier outputs are binary per step, use</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}^{(j)}\;=\;\begin{cases}\hat{\rho}_{1}-1,&amp;\tilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}=0,\\
\hat{\rho}_{1},&amp;\tilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}=1,\end{cases}\qquad A_{i,t}\ \leftarrow\ \sum_{\mathrm{index}_{i}(j)\geq t}\ \big(w_{i}^{(j)}\,\widetilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.611em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>index</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}^{(j)}\;=\;\begin{cases}\hat{\rho}_{1}-1,&amp;\tilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}=0,\\
\hat{\rho}_{1},&amp;\tilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}=1,\end{cases}\qquad A_{i,t}\ \leftarrow\ \sum_{\mathrm{index}_{i}(j)\geq t}\ \big(w_{i}^{(j)}\,\widetilde{r}_{i}^{(j)}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">If only a <em id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">final</em> binary reward is available, use a single sample-level weight <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all steps of <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (as in outcome supervision) after the standard process accumulation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Practical notes.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(i) <span id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Where to hook.</span> Implement the corrections exactly at the interface where GRPO converts rewards to (group-)normalized advantages; no change to sampling, clipping, optimizer, or KL regularization. (ii) <span id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stability.</span> Backward correction can inflate variance when <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\hat{\rho}_{0}-\hat{\rho}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\hat{\rho}_{0}-\hat{\rho}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is small; GRPO’s group normalization mitigates scale but not variance—use <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and EMA’d statistics as in practice. (iii) <span id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward variant.</span> Because group normalization is a positive rescaling, post-normalization multiplication by <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the intended gradient-direction property from the REINFORCE analysis while keeping the rest of GRPO intact. Open-source GRPO implementations follow this decomposition (reward<math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>advantage, then PPO-style surrogate + KL loss).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs and Derivations</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Connection between Corrupted Rewards and True Rewards). ‣ 3 Problem Setup and Algorithms ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We compute the expectation of the noisy reward <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on the clean reward <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a binary variable. By the definition of expectation:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tilde{R}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tilde{R}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1\cdot\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*})+0\cdot\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1\cdot\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*})+0\cdot\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">We can expand this using the law of total probability, conditioning on the value of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{*}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{*}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tilde{R}\mid R^{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tilde{R}\mid R^{*}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=R^{*}\cdot\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=1)+(1-R^{*})\cdot\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=0)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=R^{*}\cdot\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=1)+(1-R^{*})\cdot\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">From Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Verifier Reward Channel). ‣ 3 Problem Setup and Algorithms ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=0)=\rho_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=0)=\rho_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*}=1)=\rho_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*}=1)=\rho_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=1)=1-\rho_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=1)=1-\rho_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting these values:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tilde{R}\mid R^{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tilde{R}\mid R^{*}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=R^{*}(1-\rho_{1})+(1-R^{*})\rho_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=R^{*}(1-\rho_{1})+(1-R^{*})\rho_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=R^{*}-\rho_{1}R^{*}+\rho_{0}-\rho_{0}R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=R^{*}-\rho_{1}R^{*}+\rho_{0}-\rho_{0}R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})R^{*}+\rho_{0}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})R^{*}+\rho_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Unbiased Reward Estimator). ‣ 3.1 Noisy Policy Gradient with Backward Correction (PGBC) ‣ 3 Problem Setup and Algorithms ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">From proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Connection between Corrupted Rewards and True Rewards). ‣ 3 Problem Setup and Algorithms ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tilde{R}\mid R^{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tilde{R}\mid R^{*}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})R^{*}+\rho_{0}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})R^{*}+\rho_{0}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the full expectation of <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widehat{R}]=\frac{\mathbb{E}[\tilde{R}\mid R^{*}]-\rho_{0}}{\,1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1}\,}=\frac{((1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})R^{*}+\rho_{0})-\rho_{0}}{\,1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1}\,}=R^{*}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widehat{R}]=\frac{\mathbb{E}[\tilde{R}\mid R^{*}]-\rho_{0}}{\,1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1}\,}=\frac{((1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})R^{*}+\rho_{0})-\rho_{0}}{\,1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1}\,}=R^{*}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">showing unbiasedness.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Conditional Expectation of Forward Weights). ‣ 3.2 Noisy Policy Gradient with Forward Correction (PGFC) ‣ 3 Problem Setup and Algorithms ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proposition states two claims about the conditional expectation of the forward weights. The weights are defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tilde{R}}\;=\;\begin{cases}w_{0}=\rho_{1}-1&amp;\text{if }\tilde{R}=0,\\
w_{1}=\rho_{1}&amp;\text{if }\tilde{R}=1.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tilde{R}}\;=\;\begin{cases}w_{0}=\rho_{1}-1&amp;\text{if }\tilde{R}=0,\\
w_{1}=\rho_{1}&amp;\text{if }\tilde{R}=1.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">The noise model provides the conditional probabilities:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*}=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*}=1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\rho_{1},\qquad\Pr(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=1)=1-\rho_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\rho_{1},\qquad\Pr(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=1)=1-\rho_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\rho_{0},\qquad\Pr(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*}=0)=1-\rho_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\rho_{0},\qquad\Pr(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*}=0)=1-\rho_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part 1: Proof of <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=1]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=1]=0</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute the expectation of <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tilde{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tilde{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on the true reward being positive (<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{*}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{*}=1</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\{0,1\}}w_{k}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=k\mid R^{*}=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\{0,1\}}w_{k}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=k\mid R^{*}=1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w_{0}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*}=1)+w_{1}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w_{0}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*}=1)+w_{1}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\rho_{1}-1)\cdot(\rho_{1})+(\rho_{1})\cdot(1-\rho_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\rho_{1}-1)\cdot(\rho_{1})+(\rho_{1})\cdot(1-\rho_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\rho_{1}^{2}-\rho_{1})+(\rho_{1}-\rho_{1}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\rho_{1}^{2}-\rho_{1})+(\rho_{1}-\rho_{1}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part 2: Proof of <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=0]=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=0]=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we compute the expectation of <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tilde{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tilde{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on the true reward being negative (<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{*}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{*}=0</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=0]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\{0,1\}}w_{k}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=k\mid R^{*}=0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k\in\{0,1\}}w_{k}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=k\mid R^{*}=0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w_{0}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*}=0)+w_{1}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w_{0}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=0\mid R^{*}=0)+w_{1}\cdot\Pr(\tilde{R}=1\mid R^{*}=0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\rho_{1}-1)\cdot(1-\rho_{0})+(\rho_{1})\cdot(\rho_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\rho_{1}-1)\cdot(1-\rho_{0})+(\rho_{1})\cdot(\rho_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\rho_{1}-\rho_{0}\rho_{1}-1+\rho_{0})+\rho_{0}\rho_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\rho_{1}-\rho_{0}\rho_{1}-1+\rho_{0})+\rho_{0}\rho_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\rho_{1}+\rho_{0}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\rho_{1}+\rho_{0}-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This proves both claims of the proposition.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Policy Gradient Correction with Only 𝜌_1). ‣ 3.2 Noisy Policy Gradient with Forward Correction (PGFC) ‣ 3 Problem Setup and Algorithms ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We want to show that <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Delta\theta]=(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\,\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Delta\theta]=(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\,\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{t=1}^{M}h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{t=1}^{M}h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}=w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}=w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. By linearity of expectation and assuming i.i.d. samples, it suffices to show this for a single sample’s contribution, <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use the law of total expectation, conditioning on the latent true reward <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{*}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{*}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[h_{t}]=\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[h_{t}]=\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}\mid R^{*}]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}\mid R^{*}]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Pr(R^{*}=1)\,\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}\mid R^{*}=1]+\Pr(R^{*}=0)\,\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}\mid R^{*}=0]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Pr(R^{*}=1)\,\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}\mid R^{*}=1]+\Pr(R^{*}=0)\,\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}\mid R^{*}=0].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">The noise process generating <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of the policy’s action generation process (which produces <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), conditional on the true reward <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we can separate the expectations:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}\mid R^{*}]=\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}]\cdot\mathbb{E}[G_{t}\mid R^{*}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}\mid R^{*}]=\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}]\cdot\mathbb{E}[G_{t}\mid R^{*}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using the results from Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Conditional Expectation of Forward Weights). ‣ 3.2 Noisy Policy Gradient with Forward Correction (PGFC) ‣ 3 Problem Setup and Algorithms ‣ Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Imperfect Verifiers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>:</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=1]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=1]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=0]=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}\mid R^{*}=0]=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these back into the main expectation formula:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Pr(R^{*}=1)\cdot(0)\cdot\mathbb{E}[G_{t}\mid R^{*}=1]+\Pr(R^{*}=0)\cdot(-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1}))\cdot\mathbb{E}[G_{t}\mid R^{*}=0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Pr(R^{*}=1)\cdot(0)\cdot\mathbb{E}[G_{t}\mid R^{*}=1]+\Pr(R^{*}=0)\cdot(-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1}))\cdot\mathbb{E}[G_{t}\mid R^{*}=0]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\cdot\Pr(R^{*}=0)\mathbb{E}[G_{t}\mid R^{*}=0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\cdot\Pr(R^{*}=0)\mathbb{E}[G_{t}\mid R^{*}=0]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\cdot\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=0\}}G_{t}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\cdot\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=0\}}G_{t}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\{\cdot\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\{\cdot\}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator function.
From two fundamental properties of the score function:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The unconditional expectation is zero: <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[G_{t}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[G_{t}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Williams, 1992</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sutton et al., 1999</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The clean policy gradient is <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}[R^{*}G_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}[R^{*}G_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">From property 1, we have <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[G_{t}]=\mathbb{E}[(\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=1\}}+\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=0\}})G_{t}]=\mathbb{E}[R^{*}G_{t}]+\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=0\}}G_{t}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[G_{t}]=\mathbb{E}[(\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=1\}}+\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=0\}})G_{t}]=\mathbb{E}[R^{*}G_{t}]+\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=0\}}G_{t}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies that <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=0\}}G_{t}]=-\mathbb{E}[R^{*}G_{t}]=-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=0\}}G_{t}]=-\mathbb{E}[R^{*}G_{t}]=-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we substitute this back into our expression for the expected update direction:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[h_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[h_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[w_{\tilde{R}}G_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\cdot\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=0\}}G_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\cdot\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{1}_{\{R^{*}=0\}}G_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\cdot(-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\cdot(-\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the expectation of the full update is <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Delta\theta]=\frac{1}{M}\sum\mathbb{E}[h_{t}]=(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Delta\theta]=\frac{1}{M}\sum\mathbb{E}[h_{t}]=(1-\rho_{0}-\rho_{1})\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Prompt Templates and Training/Evaluation Details</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section records the exact prompt formats and the concrete hyperparameters we used for all experiments in <em id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable yet Noisy Rewards under Unreliable Verifiers</em>. We mirror the level of detail used in recent RLVR appendices and report settings sufficient for full reproducibility from our released code.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Prompt Templates</h3>

<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training (generation) prompt.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each math problem <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> (a plain-text question), the user message is built by concatenating the raw question with a short instruction that elicits chain-of-thought and enforces a verifiable answer format.</p>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64,PHVzZXI+CntRVUVTVElPTn0KCkxldCdzIHRoaW5rIHN0ZXAgYnkgc3RlcCBhbmQgZW5jbG9zZSB0aGUgcmVhc29uaW5nIHByb2Nlc3Mgd2l0aGluIDx0aGluaz4gYW5kIDwvdGhpbms+IHRhZ3MuClRoZSBmaW5hbCByZXN1bHQgaW4gdGhlIGFuc3dlciBNVVNUIEJFIHdpdGhpbiBcYm94ZWR7fS4KPC91c2VyPg==" download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;</span><span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">user</span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&gt;</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{</span><span id="lstnumberx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">QUESTION</span><span id="lstnumberx4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">}</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx5" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Let</span><span id="lstnumberx6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’</span><span id="lstnumberx6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">s</span><span id="lstnumberx6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">think</span><span id="lstnumberx6.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">step</span><span id="lstnumberx6.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">by</span><span id="lstnumberx6.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">step</span><span id="lstnumberx6.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">and</span><span id="lstnumberx6.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">enclose</span><span id="lstnumberx6.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">the</span><span id="lstnumberx6.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">reasoning</span><span id="lstnumberx6.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">process</span><span id="lstnumberx6.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">within</span><span id="lstnumberx6.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;</span><span id="lstnumberx6.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">think</span><span id="lstnumberx6.27" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&gt;</span><span id="lstnumberx6.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">and</span><span id="lstnumberx6.30" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.31" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/</span><span id="lstnumberx6.32" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">think</span><span id="lstnumberx6.33" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&gt;</span><span id="lstnumberx6.34" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.35" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">tags</span><span id="lstnumberx6.36" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">The</span><span id="lstnumberx7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">final</span><span id="lstnumberx7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">result</span><span id="lstnumberx7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">in</span><span id="lstnumberx7.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">the</span><span id="lstnumberx7.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">answer</span><span id="lstnumberx7.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">MUST</span><span id="lstnumberx7.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">BE</span><span id="lstnumberx7.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">within</span><span id="lstnumberx7.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\</span><span id="lstnumberx7.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">boxed</span><span id="lstnumberx7.21" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{}.</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/</span><span id="lstnumberx8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">user</span><span id="lstnumberx8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&gt;</span>
</div>
</div>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">During data preprocessing, we write chat-style JSON with a single user turn as shown above and attach the rule-based ground-truth answer for reward checking.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation (validation/test) prompt.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the same prompt template as training for validation and test-time generation so that the rule-based verifier can parse the boxed answer consistently.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Verifier I/O.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rule-based</span> checker operates on the model’s final string and extracts the last <code id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">\boxed{...}</code> expression; it then applies numeric/rational parsing and equality tests to produce a binary reward <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When the <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM verifier</span> is enabled, it receives the pair <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{problem},\text{model solution})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>problem</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>model solution</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{problem},\text{model solution})</annotation></semantics></math> and returns a binary correctness decision used only to estimate the false negative rate <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> over a sliding window. The LLM verifier does not replace the rule-based reward.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Data Preprocessing</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We load the preview split of the math-reasoning corpus and map each example to a chat-style record as above, keeping the reference (ground-truth) answer for programmatic checking.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Training Configuration</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless otherwise stated, all runs use GRPO (outcome supervision) with the following constants.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training (GRPO)</span></td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Train batch size</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">128</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Rollouts per question (group size)</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">8</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Max prompt length (tokens)</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">512</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Max response length (tokens)</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">3072</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Sampling temperature (rollouts)</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">1.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Advantage estimator</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Group-normalized (GRPO)</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">KL regularization</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Enabled</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">KL coefficient <math id="A4.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.001</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Entropy coefficient</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Optimizer</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">AdamW</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Learning rate</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">3e-6</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T3.2.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Total epochs</td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">1</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Core training settings.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model/backbone.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We load the base model from local cache (HuggingFace layout), enable FSDP2 for actor/ref, and use shared-memory weights with remove-padding for efficient vLLM rollouts. The KL is computed w.r.t. a frozen reference initialized from the same base.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Datasets</h3>

<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DeepScaleR</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2025</a>)</cite>: the math-reasoning corpus used for RLVR rollouts and policy updates.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate with the standard official/problem releases for each benchmark and apply the same rule-based programmatic checking protocol throughout.</p>
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MATH500</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lightman et al., 2023</a>)</cite>: a verifiable subset of math reasoning problems for reliable evaluation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AIME 2024</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">HuggingFaceH4, 2024</a>)</cite>: the 2024 American Invitational Mathematics Examination set.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AIME 2025</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenCompass, 2025</a>)</cite>: the 2025 AIME set.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AMC 2023</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">math-ai, 2025</a>)</cite>: problems from the 2023 American Mathematics Competitions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Minerva Math</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lewkowycz et al., 2022</a>)</cite>: the Minerva math evaluation suite.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OlympiadBench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2024</a>)</cite>: olympiad-level mathematics benchmark.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>False Positive (FP) and False Negative (FN) Examples</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide FP and FN examples using Qwen2.5-Math-7B base model on MATH 500.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">FP</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">    </span><span id="lstnumberx10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"</span><span id="lstnumberx10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">idx</span><span id="lstnumberx10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">":</span><span id="lstnumberx10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">16,</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">    </span><span id="lstnumberx11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"</span><span id="lstnumberx11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">question</span><span id="lstnumberx11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">":</span><span id="lstnumberx11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"</span><span id="lstnumberx11.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Compute</span><span id="lstnumberx11.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span><span id="lstnumberx11.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">$1</span><span id="lstnumberx11.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">-2+3-4+5-</span><span id="lstnumberx11.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\\</span><span id="lstnumberx11.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">dots</span><span id="lstnumberx11.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">+99-100</span><span id="lstnumberx11.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">$</span><span id="lstnumberx11.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.",</span>
</div>
